    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `title` \u2192 `salutation` feature following the codebase's existing conventions for owner fields and derived read-only values.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `title` as an optional input field on `OwnerFields` (enum `MR`/`MRS`/`MS`/`DR`), and `salutation` as a read-only derived field on `Owner`. The DTOs are code-generated from this spec at build time.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the persisted `title` column (getter/setter) and a `@Transient getSalutation()` that returns `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when the title is null/blank.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added the `title` column to the `owners` table. The tests run on the `hsqldb` profile.\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` needed no changes: `title` auto-maps (String \u2194 generated enum) in both directions, and `salutation` auto-maps from `getSalutation()` onto the response DTO \u2014 mirroring how existing derived fields like `displayName` flow through.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComposesSalutation` (POST an owner with `title=DR`, `lastName=who`, then GET expecting `salutation` = `\"DR who\"`) passes.",
